{
  "title": "Concurrent Retry requests can run one scrape job twice",
  "description": "retry_job (server/src/scraping/runner.rs) checks `status == failed` on a loaded row, then runs an UPDATE that doesn't re-check the status. \
Two Retry requests that arrive together (double tap, web and iOS at once) both pass the check, and api/scrape/retry.rs calls spawn_scrape_job twice, so the same job runs its steps twice, including the AI enrichment and apply steps. \
Fix: add `.filter(status.eq(STATUS_FAILED))` to the reset UPDATE and treat 0 rows updated as InvalidState, so only one request spawns the job. \
Add an e2e test that fires two retries concurrently and checks one job run (for example via the mock AI call counts).",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "api",
    "scraping",
  ],
